Z||000000||FieroKyle||11-18-2001||10:08 PM||||Alright, I was at the Goodyear dealer just window shopping. I saw these ones that I really like. It was closed but they said "PSW" on the center cap. What I am asking is that 1. is there a website for this company, and 2. does anyone have this brand and have expierence on the quality, also 3. what do these run in prices. If someone knew there home site I could show ya guys what I am looking at, and I could get prices and sizes.<P>Another thing, is hard to get 14'' x 215 like the original rims on the Fiero (85 GT). I usually only see 15'' on up. I plan on getting some lowering springs to get the wheel well space outta there so I am not concerned that they are only 14s. Plus I have a lot money on the set of tires thats on them and they are brand new. I don't wanna turn around and have to get new tires on a car. And since I only put on about 8k miles a year on the car, 60k tires are gonna last a while. Anyways, just telling ya guys I know nothing about rims on far as whats expensive and whats good on the market. I don't know brands are what ya want and blah blah blah, Alls I am looking for is looks because that.<P>Anyways with the Fiero in storage all winter I can save my money. Thanks guys for any input on this.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
